(561086, 56591, 16352, '<td valign="top">Difficult to make a shot like this look original. It has been done so often. What lifts this one is that you have retained the beautiful chestnut -  and there is just enough depth of field. The shape of the pupil is beautiful. I would not normally like an eye so close to the centre of the picture - it totally destroys the rule of thirds BUT I have tried cropping this in every way imaginable and not one looked as good as this. I think that proved that rules like that are (at times) made to be broken.<br/>David<br/></td>', 'Difficult to make a shot like this look original. It has been done so often. What lifts this one is that you have retained the beautiful chestnut -  and there is just enough depth of field. The shape of the pupil is beautiful. I would not normally like an eye so close to the centre of the picture - it totally destroys the rule of thirds BUT I have tried cropping this in every way imaginable and not one looked as good as this. I think that proved that rules like that are (at times) made to be broken.David', '2004-01-28 17:45:51.000000', NULL, 1),
